WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.566
Hi there! Who are you?

2
00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:15.949
I'm a red kangaroo.

3
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:20.582
Red kangaroos are marsupials.

4
00:00:20.583 --> 00:00:28.482
Female marsupials carry their babies in pouches.

5
00:00:28.483 --> 00:00:31.451
Where do you live?

6
00:00:31.452 --> 00:00:36.149
Red kangaroos live in Australia.

7
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:46.017
We like open grasslands and deserts.

8
00:00:46.018 --> 00:00:51.472
Oh! I see your baby!

9
00:00:51.473 --> 00:00:55.014
He's called a joey.

10
00:00:55.015 --> 00:00:59.882
Joeys sometimes come out to explore.

11
00:00:59.883 --> 00:01:10.105
After ten months they leave the pouch forever.

12
00:01:10.106 --> 00:01:13.741
What do you eat?

13
00:01:13.742 --> 00:01:19.227
Red kangaroos eat grass and leaves.

14
00:01:19.228 --> 00:01:24.462
We can last for several days without water.

15
00:01:24.463 --> 00:01:29.443
Do kangaroos really box?

16
00:01:29.444 --> 00:01:35.147
Male kangaroos often fight with their front paws.

17
00:01:35.148 --> 00:01:41.184
They also kick with their back legs.

18
00:01:41.185 --> 00:01:47.775
Do you have any enemies?

19
00:01:47.776 --> 00:01:54.411
Wild dogs called dingoes hunt us.

20
00:01:54.412 --> 00:02:01.426
We stomp our feet when danger is near.

21
00:02:01.427 --> 00:02:07.829
Your feet are long!

22
00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:11.526
Our feet are very strong too.

23
00:02:11.527 --> 00:02:15.737
They help us jump far.

24
00:02:15.738 --> 00:02:24.722
Red kangaroos can jump up to 12 meters!

25
00:02:24.723 --> 00:02:28.118
Uh-oh. I see a dingo!

26
00:02:28.119 --> 00:02:33.071
Good day!

27
00:02:33.072 --> 00:02:39.907
Good-bye, Red Kangaroo!

